window.PK_MERGES=["Aksum was written up three times; the full account now sits on Africa’s knowledge and its journeys, with a short pointer on What was taken and lost and a dated marker on the world timeline.", "Civil service representation appeared in near-identical words on Through other lenses and the DEEIA lens; the DEEIA page now gives only the parity comparison and links to the full breakdown.", "Black Equity Organisation and the Ubele Initiative were described identically as networks and as partners; each entry now says why it appears in both places.", "Black Cultural Archives: the archives list now points to the learning offer on the schools page instead of repeating it.", "Thirty pairs of sections on different pages that cover the same ground now link to each other both ways.", "Menus: What was taken, lost and might have been moved to Learn, next to Africa’s knowledge and its journeys; The African diaspora moved to Understand, next to What it means to be Black.", "New page: Who built the stereotypes, and what they cost (Learn), linked both ways to the narratives on What was taken, the ethics section of the DNA page, the language page, myths, young lives and the life-course lens, so nothing is said twice.", "Kept apart on purpose: the overview’s spotlights (Le Morne, San Basilio de Palenque, Afro-Mexican recognition) are short teasers that link to the full diaspora entries; the inequalities, life stages and young lives pages serve different readers and now link to each other rather than merge."];
